Article 3 Unless otherwise provided by the finance and tax competent departments of the State Council, the following income, regardless of whether the place of payment is within the territory of China, shall be income sourced from within the territory of China:
(1) income from providing labor services within the territory of China due to employment, engagement, or performance of contracts, etc.;
(2) income from leasing property to a lessee for use within the territory of China;
(3) income from licensing various franchise rights for use within the territory of China;
(4) income from transferring real property within the territory of China or other property transferred within the territory of China;
(5) income from interest, dividends, and bonuses derived from enterprises, public institutions, other organizations, and resident individuals within the territory of China.

Article 16. The original value of property as specified in Item 5 of Paragraph 1 of Article 6 of the Individual Income Tax Law shall be determined according to the following methods:
(1) For marketable securities, it shall be the purchase price and the relevant fees paid at the time of purchase in accordance with regulations;
(2) For buildings, it shall be the construction cost or purchase price and other relevant expenses;
(3) For land use rights, it shall be the amount paid for obtaining the land use rights, expenses for land development, and other relevant expenses;
(4) For machinery, equipment, vehicles, and vessels, it shall be the purchase price, transportation expenses, installation expenses, and other relevant expenses.
For other property, the original value shall be determined by reference to the methods prescribed in the preceding paragraph.
If a taxpayer fails to provide complete and accurate documentary evidence of the original value of property and cannot determine the original value according to the methods prescribed in Paragraph 1 of this Article, the competent tax authority shall assess the original value of the property.
The term "reasonable expenses" as referred to in Item 5 of Paragraph 1 of Article 6 of the Individual Income Tax Law means the relevant taxes and fees paid in accordance with regulations when selling the property.

Article 25 Circumstances requiring annual settlement for comprehensive income include:
(1) obtaining comprehensive income from two or more sources and the balance of annual comprehensive income after deducting special deductions exceeds RMB 60,000;
(2) obtaining one or more types of income from remuneration for personal services, author's remuneration, or royalties, and the balance of annual comprehensive income after deducting special deductions exceeds RMB 60,000;
(3) the amount of tax withheld and paid in the tax year is lower than the amount of tax payable;
(4) the taxpayer applies for a tax refund.
A taxpayer applying for a tax refund shall provide a bank account opened within China and process the tax refund at the place of annual settlement.
The specific measures for annual settlement shall be formulated by the competent tax authority under the State Council.
